#
# libstdc++ <format> stores "no precision" as `size_t __prec = -1` inside
# _M_get_precision (GCC 15: libstdc++-v3/include/std/format). Clang's
# implicit-integer-sign-change check reports that conversion. The function is
# inlined into the caller, so a fun: entry does not match the frame that is
# emitted; the source location is still the <format> header.
#
# This list ignores only that check in that header. AddressSanitizer and every
# other UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer check still instrument <format>, and
# implicit-integer-sign-change still fires in every other file.

[implicit-integer-sign-change]
src:*/c++/*/format
